		Annotation {
		  SID			  "1990:373"
		  Name			  "Per Aaron Shatters:\nThis filter was added to PCS (the CPM predecessor) because pump piston pass frequen"
		  "cy was aliasing into the signal.  Being kind of like a discrete derivative, the variance calculation is sensitive "
		  "to high frequency noise.  So this filter was added to prevent the high frequency instances of this noise.  Being a"
		  " two sample moving average, it is the fastest filter that eliminated the noise.  It was not thoroughly technically"
		  " examined, but it worked.  It's not clear the extent to which this is necessary here, since Pseudo-Frictionless We"
		  "igh works only when the tilt and lift valve command is zero, so the pump should not be hydraulically connected to "
		  "the cylinder at this time.  The pump is also likely to be at a low stroke, so piston pass ripple amplitude should "
		  "be low."
		  Position		  [-82, 98, 297, 234]
		  InternalMargins	  [0, 0, 0, 0]
		  FixedHeight		  on
		  FixedWidth		  on
		  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
		  VerticalAlignment	  "top"
		  ZOrder		  -1
		}
	      }
	    }
